<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .inside-iran p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">October 9, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 224 of the 2026 Iran-US Conflict</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-10-09T07:00:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v49.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      The near-term diplomatic test — whether Iran formally responds to the US counter-proposal before October 12 (<span class="cite">F8</span>, p=0.58) — runs on a parallel track with the post-midterm escalation window extending to November 10 (<span class="cite">F11</span>, p=0.35), and how the first resolves will directly condition the second.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">6 active · 4 resolved today · last reasoned 2026-10-09</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-Term · ≤72h</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8 · 2026-10-09-iran-formal-response-us-counterproposal-by-oct12</span>
          <span class="fc-category">Diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran publicly convey a formal governmental response to the US counter-proposal on the seven-day Hormuz plan before EOD 2026-10-12?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">58%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New today (p₀ = 58%)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-12</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 72h forecast. Foreign Minister Araghchi stated on October 8 that Iran had received Washington's counter-response to the seven-day Hormuz plan and was reviewing it, with a reply expected "within a few days." Three days is a plausible timeline for a formal written counter, given Iran's history of maintaining formal diplomatic contact even through adversarial phases and the implicit expectation Araghchi set publicly. Against: Pezeshkian simultaneously called talks "meaningless," and hardliner resistance to a substantive reply is documented. Base tilts above 0.5 because the Araghchi framing set a near-term public expectation that a non-response would itself constitute a strategic message.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>A statement by a named senior Iranian official (Araghchi, Pezeshkian, or Baghaei) relayed through a named mediator OR published by IRNA/PressTV/Tasnim, confirming transmission of a formal Iranian position document to US counterparts, before EOD 2026-10-12 UTC.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Must appear in at least one of: Reuters, AP, AFP, Al Jazeera, Iran International, or an official Iranian government spokesperson statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Vague public statements ('talks continue') without confirmation of formal document transmission do not resolve YES. Only a specific claim of a formal written or diplomatic note transmitted to US counterparts counts.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Araghchi press conference announcing formal reply sent</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar FM statement confirming receipt of Iranian formal response</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRNA dispatch confirming SNSC meeting outcome on US counter-proposal</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 Days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9 · 2026-10-09-iran-us-ceasefire-or-hormuz-deal-by-oct17</span>
          <span class="fc-category">Diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US and Iran announce a new formal ceasefire or Strait of Hormuz reopening agreement before EOD 2026-10-17?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">7%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New today (p₀ = 7%)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-17</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 8-day forecast. Structural conditions strongly disfavor a deal within 8 days: Trump rejected Iran's Sep 24 seven-day plan as insufficient; Pezeshkian called talks "meaningless"; the US military has completed preparations for potential resumed strikes. The two prior ceasefires (April, June) each collapsed within weeks; a third would require political capital neither side currently shows. Residual probability (0.07) accounts for the possibility of a surprise back-channel breakthrough mediated by Qatar or Pakistan, given Trump's history of sudden dealmaking announcements.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>A joint or parallel announcement by US and Iranian governments of a formal ceasefire, Hormuz reopening agreement, or equivalent diplomatic instrument confirmed by at least two of the listed mediator governments (Qatar, Pakistan, Egypt).</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters AND at least one of AP or AFP must confirm.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Unilateral declarations, 'productive talks' statements, or proposals still under review do not count. Must be a confirmed bilateral agreement with mediator corroboration.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar FM emergency travel to Washington or Tehran announced</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump-Pezeshkian direct phone call announced by either side</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US executive order on Iranian asset freeze or sanction waiver announced</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5 · 2026-09-03-likud-plurality-oct27-election</span>
          <span class="fc-category">Domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Likud win the most Knesset seats (seat plurality) in the October 27, 2026 Israeli election?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">30%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −12pp from 42% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">UPDATE (36-day gap). DA opposing narrative accepted by Judge: four of five major Israeli pollsters now show Eisenkot's Yashar party holding a plurality, reversing the near-tie picture from early September. Channel 13 (Sep 23): Yashar 22 seats, Likud 18. Channel 12: Yashar 24, Likud 23. Kan: Yashar 24, Likud 23. Maariv: tie 21-21. The lone outlier is i24NEWS showing Likud 27, Yashar 22. PM preference: Eisenkot leads 48% vs Netanyahu 36% (Channel 13, Oct 2026). p reduced 0.42 → 0.30. Complementary forecast F10 (Yashar plurality) set at p=0.52; F5+F10=0.82, residual 0.18 covers third-party plurality scenarios.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if official Knesset election results published by the Israeli Central Elections Committee show Likud winning more seats than any other single party in the October 27, 2026 election.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Israeli Central Elections Committee official results, carried by Times of Israel/Haaretz/Reuters/AP.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If Likud and one other party tie on seats: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO (no plurality). Exit polls alone do not resolve; official preliminary results suffice if published before EOD Oct 27.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-CONTRADICTED">Polls showing Likud ≥23 seats, ahead of Yashar across Channel 12/13/Kan</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Likud bloc forms coalition-eligible alliance pre-election</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Eisenkot/Yashar polling surge above 25 seats in multiple polls</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F10 · 2026-10-09-yashar-plurality-oct27-election</span>
          <span class="fc-category">Domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Eisenkot's Yashar party win the most Knesset seats (plurality) in the October 27, 2026 Israeli election?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">52%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New today (p₀ = 52%)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast complementary to F5 (Likud plurality). Yashar leads in four of five recent major polls (Channel 12: 24 vs 23; Channel 13: 22 vs 18; Kan: 24 vs 23; Maariv: tied 21-21), with i24 as the only outlier favoring Likud. Eisenkot leads on PM preference by 12 points. F5 (Likud) + F10 (Yashar) = 0.30 + 0.52 = 0.82; residual ~0.18 covers third-party plurality scenarios. Three weeks remain; the race is volatile with neither bloc near a 61-seat majority.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>Yashar wins more Knesset seats than any other single party in the official certified results published by the Israeli Central Elections Committee for the Oct 27, 2026 election.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Official Central Elections Committee results or confirmed by Times of Israel, Haaretz, and at least one international wire service.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>In case of a perfect tie in seat count between Yashar and another party, resolve AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Preliminary or exit poll results alone do not resolve; official preliminary results suffice if published before EOD Oct 27.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Three or more polls Oct 13–20 showing Yashar 24+ seats, ahead of Likud</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Gideon Sa'ar's Together party or Democrats consolidate above electoral threshold</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-regime status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F12 · 2026-10-09-mojtaba-khamenei-public-appearance-by-oct31</span>
          <span class="fc-category">Regime</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Mojtaba Khamenei make a confirmed public video or audio appearance before EOD 2026-10-31?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New today (p₀ = 22%)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-31</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 22-day forecast. Mojtaba Khamenei has not appeared publicly since the war began in late February 2026 — over 7 months of absence. Iranian state media (Mehr, IRNA, Tasnim) have circulated undated archival video and a reportedly handwritten letter to fill the leadership visibility gap. Pezeshkian claimed a 7-8 hour meeting with Khamenei, implying he is alive and functioning, but IRIB has not produced authenticated post-war footage. INSS assessed that Mojtaba's legitimacy gap is a live internal vulnerability. p=0.22 reflects compound uncertainty: whether he is in condition to appear, and whether the regime would judge an appearance strategically advantageous before Oct 31 given authentication risks.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>A live or recorded appearance where Mojtaba Khamenei is visibly or aurally present, carrying metadata or context authenticating it as post-February 28, 2026, confirmed by at least two independent international analysts or outlets (not solely IRNA/Mehr/Tasnim).</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Iran International OR BBC Persian combined with at least one Western wire service (Reuters/AP/AFP) must authenticate.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Photographs without video or audio context, handwritten letters, or second-hand accounts of meetings do not count. IRIB-only releases without independent international authentication do not resolve YES.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRIB scheduling announcement referencing a Mojtaba Khamenei address or statement</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">State-linked social media activity referencing an upcoming Mojtaba appearance</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Pezeshkian public reference to a recent verified meeting with the leader</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F11 · 2026-10-09-trump-announces-resumed-iran-strikes-by-nov10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">Military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Trump publicly announce that the US will resume or has resumed large-scale military strikes on Iran before EOD 2026-11-10?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">35%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New today (p₀ = 35%)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-11-10</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 32-day forecast. Trump told aides he expects to launch fresh strikes after the November 3 midterms (Wall Street Journal, Sep 26); the US military has completed preparations for potential resumed operations with no date given (CNBC, Oct 8). Trump's pre-midterm pledge explicitly removes the timetable through November 3, leaving a 7-day post-election window before November 10. Against: Iran and the US remain in indirect talks through Qatar; Rubio described "progress" on October 8. p=0.35 reflects the post-midterm announcement risk without overweighting the brief Nov 3-10 window.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>A confirmed public statement by Trump, the White House, or Pentagon that the US has resumed or will resume large-scale (not defensive or routine) strikes on Iran, issued before EOD Nov 10, 2026.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>White House statement or confirmed simultaneously by Reuters AND Associated Press.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Defensive or small-scale retaliatory strikes without explicit 'resumption' framing do not resolve YES. Pentagon's unilateral characterization of any strike as 'defensive' counts as NO for this forecast.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">November 3 midterm results — strong Republican showing providing political cover</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">New Iranian attack on US assets between Oct 9 and Nov 10</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump post-midterm press conference language on Iran (hostile vs. deal-seeking)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 6-12 MONTHS -->
